Telecinco closed with an increase of 2.54 per cent yesterday.
This increase puts its annual losses at 15.66 percent.
Fifty-five per cent of the company belong to Mediaset and 13 per cent to Vocento, so according to Bloomberg’s data it is 4.48.88.88 million.
Rivical Antena 3 lost 1.52 per cent yesterday and has seen a 40.5 per cent drop since January, up from 2.193.46 per cent yesterday.
The value of the other subscribed communication companies for Sogecable is 3,571 million; 2.518.53 million for Prisa (the publisher of Cinco Días) and 1.779 million for Vocento.
According to Vasile, the comparison with Antena 3 is due to the similarities between the two companies.
The only question is how much we can perform in the same market, at what cost, and how it pays off in terms of viewership.
Telecinco announced last week that they would like to be the first TV channel of more than 1 billion in gross advertising revenue this year, said Giuseppe Tringali, acting adviser at Telecinco and Publiespasa. The latter is the group’s advertising subsidiary.
If the announced fact were realised, compared to 965.4 million recorded in the financial year in the financial year 2006, the TV channel would increase its advertising revenue by 3.6 percent this fiscal year.
Antena’s 3 net turnover increased by 1.6 percent in the first nine months of the financial year (around 734.4 million), while television’s net sales increased by 0.7 percent (630,4 million).
