Congress Approves Recreation of MiFID, which came into effect on November 1.
Simultaneously with the parliamentary process, which ended today with a controversial vote approving the amendments of the senate, the government initiated a social dialogue on the regulation underlying the law, so that both could come into effect before the end of the end of the year.
Deputies from different groups unanimously underlined the efforts of MPs and senators invested in talks and agreements to create the most favorable standards for investors, as well as a detailed regulation of the activities of companies in order to operate efficiently on the market.
Mifid, which amends the Securities Markets Act, makes it possible to modernize the financial markets, at the same time strengthens the protection of investors, broadens the supervisory rights of the Spanish National Securities Markets Commission (CNMV) and promotes cooperation between the various superintendents of the European Union.
The new directive will allow financial consultancy services for specialised companies, but also natural or legal persons, as well as securities distribution companies, securities agencies and portfolio management companies (ESIS), namely financial advisory companies (AFI).
In addition, the law will increase the number of systems suitable for carrying out operations involving funds, in such a way, multilateral trading platforms and internalisation systems for the execution of assignments are added to regulated secondary markets.
In addition, the Act obliges investment service providers to provide market information regarding the decisive aspects of their business profile, their risk-taking and risk-management methods, as well as to maintain CNMV’s control of the CNMV, we must keep a record of all completed operations.
The Economic Committee of Congress has enshrined a number of modifications. Of these, it is of paramount importance that securitised debts are treated as “complex” funds, due to the high-profile risk posed by the investor’s high-risk mortgage lending.
On the other hand, the transposition of the directive has also been harnessed by legally outlining the scope of activities of economic and enterpris-educated. 30 years after the Royal Decree defining the professional functions that can only be performed by economists came into force in 1977.
The Senate proposed the creation of new players in the financial sector, such as the intermediary’s agent, who works for another account, does not need the CNMV’s permission, and can market products or obtain customers for several investment companies at the same time.
The Consumer Indication increased by 0.5 points in November, reaching 4.1%.
This indicator, taken into account by Eurostat to calculate the inflation rate of the European Union, shows the evolution of prices in Spain for the month of November.
Disclosure complies with Eurostat’s and the European Central Bank’s strategy to provide data that is comparable to data coming from the United States, both in terms of the time and nature of their creation.
For the preliminary indicator, the same method of calculation is used to calculate the Unqualified Commodity Indicator, but the statistical modelling method differs in estimating the information that is not yet available at the time of disclosure.
The Statistical Office emphasized that the preliminary indicator is purely informative, so it may deviate from the final data, which will be published on 14 December.
"The Consumer Price Indication continues to show a relatively high value."
Pedro Solbes, vice-president of the government (Government and Minister of Economy), stated that an increase in the Consumer Price Indicator to 4.1% in November is “temporary in nature”, but at the same time predicted that the price index is expected to show a “relatively high value” in the coming months.
In the Corridors of the Parliament, Solbes reaffirmed that “While the indicator is not really favourable”, the inflation rate in Spain has remained more or less at the same level within the monetary union in recent years.
He also added that the month in November “was less surprise” than in the previous month, when the government did not expect such a large increase.
“We expected a value of around 4%,” the Minister of Economic Affairs acknowledged in connection with the data published today.
Northern Rock aims to reach 42 billion euros in three-season years.
Northern Rock deposits have fallen by more than 50% and are currently only 12 billion pounds (EUR 1,600 million) since it came into crisis in mid-September to take out an urgent loan from the National Bank of England.
At the same time, he still had a record number of deposits of more than 25 billion pounds, the number of which gradually declined over the past two-and-a-half months due to the loss of customer confidence, despite the fact that the Government promised the bank a one-hundred-dollar guarantee until the end of the crisis.
U.S., under its own financial and commercial name, will operate this unit under the name Virgin Money. Virgin will have to acquire about a quarter of the British bank’s revenue over the next three years in order to get the remaining 18 billion pounds to reach the EUR 30 billion target.
Famous businessman Richard Branson’s group, known for his high-profile advertising campaigns in England, intends to spend about 50 million pound (i.e. 70 million euros a year) on advertising and marketing in order to achieve his goal.
Earlier this week, Northern Rock lifted the Virgin consortium’s offer as the most favorable to avoid bankruptcies. In addition to Virgin, the consortium consists of three other companies.
Totana mayor Arrested for Suspected Corruption Prosecution
Earlier this morning, the Gendarmerie Arrested the mayor of Totana (Nopia in the Murcia province) suspected of being involved in an urban corruption scandal that erupted this week.
One of the secretaries of the City Hall and the police chief of the town was arrested.
José Martínez Andreo, a member of the city council, took the place of Juan Morales, a member of the European People’s Party in May, according to official bodies interviewed by the SER radio channel.
The police continue to investigate the city’s offices and the Urban Development Council, and it cannot be ruled out that further arrests are expected.
Juan Moral’s lawyer has also been investigated as the main suspect in the corruption scandal that erupted this week.
