What insurance suits me?
Car insurance, which means security for the owner of the vehicle, entails a significant expense compared to various damage events and depends on a number of factors, such as the age, gender, the date of obtaining a driving licence, marritic status, the type of vehicle to be insured and the nature of its use.
Purchasing a car is only a first step.
Choosing the right insurance is often more difficult than deciding what kind of car you would like.
First of all, we need to be aware of what this is all about.
Car insurance is an agreement between the insurance company and the insurer.
This agreement is embodied in the form of an insurance contract, which stipulates that the insured company undertakes compensation for the fixed insurance premium in the event of the occurrence.
The insurance premium is practically the amount paid for insurance, which is determined taking into account various factors, such as age, gender, date of obtaining a driving licence, marital status, the type of car to be insured, its utilization, etc.
The insurance companies determine the insurance premium on the basis of the statistics, i.e. a higher amount is paid by those who represent a higher risk of an accident.
That’s why people over the age of more than 25 or women pay less, because according to statistics, they pose a lower risk because they are more cautious.
Similarly, according to the reports, insurance corporations have come to the conclusion that people living in marriage also cause fewer accidents than solitary people.
Frequency is decisive for the type of use of the car.
The possibility of an accident is more common.
A number of factors are taken into account by insurance companies when determining the insurance premium.
Therefore, the owner should carefully look into it so that he can choose the most appropriate form of insurance for his profile.
In the following, we present the most important factors for the choice, so that it is best to adapt to the needs of the insured and create an acceptable price.
When concluding an insurance contract, people under the age of 25 have to face a number of disadvantages, such as the lack of driving experience and the freshness of a driving licence.
“While it’s most ideal to be insured against every threat, there are also more economical solutions.
Supplier leaders can take out complete insurance with self-sufficient self-sufficient, thereby ensuring against all hazards, and the price will also be affordable.
For this type of contract, the insured person pays part of the damage.
“The amount of deductibility payable by the insured depends on the insurance premium; the higher the premium, the lower the deductible,” says Luis Noguera, Head of First Europa’s Intermediary on Internet Insurance in Spain.
Another option is liability insurance enlarged for third parties, when the customer insures himself against the damage caused to others, but not the damage done in his own car.
In addition, it will be ensured against the theft, fire damage and the loss of the car.
It's a piece of advice.
If you’re not already 25 years old, be cautious and preferably avoid accustoming, because it affects the bonus and you’ll be able to reduce the amounts payable in the future.
A bonus is referred to the discounts provided in relation to the insurance company’s base rate.
Punishment against the basic tariff is called a foliage.
“The amount of the bonus and pendant depends on the insurance company and its profits.
“If it’s been a good year for the company, you’ll be able to afford to increase your bonus,” Noguera explains.
Once the age limit of up to the age of 25, it is easier for the owners to take out adequate insurance, as the risk of an accustomed decreases due to the experience gained over the years.
At this time, we are advising you to take out a complete insufficiency with self-sufficiency.
“Usually, young people are not yet able to use their experiences properly in an accident or even when driving,” says the director of the European insurance company in Spain, adding that the majority of accidents will occur in the second year of management, when the drivers have already outperformed their differences.
If the insurer is already married but does not yet have children, it’s best to take out a complete insurance, of course if its financial options allow it.
Insurance associations consider married couples with a child as customers with the lowest risk, so the fee to be paid is also lower in their case.
In this case, it’s best to self-sufficient self-sufficient (which can reach 300 euros), or if they have a higher bonus, they can extend the insurance from the third year of the vehicle to the damage caused to someone else.
“They drive more calmly, but at the same time they have a greater purchasing power and they can afford to have a higher deductible,” confirms Luis Nogue.
In the case of pensioners, we recommend complete insurance with self-sufficiency (which is around 150 euros), or in the case of a higher bonus, it can also be extended to liability insurance.
Automobile insurance is a very important thing, not only because it means protection for the owner in the event of damage events, but also because it means a big expense, so it is essential to choose the personalized form of insurance properly.
